<http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00000385> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                  owl:versionIRI <http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00000385> ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/conforms_to_gpad> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/modelstate> "development" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8769-177X" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date> "2026-10-20"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "GOLPH3-dependent intra-Golgi recycling of glycosphingolipid synthases (Human)"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/pav/providedBy> "http://geneontology.org"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "2026-10-20: PI4KB activity unit removed (no paper shows PI4KB acting on GOLPH3; link rested on inhibitor/yeast data). Replaced by PI4P (CHEBI:58178) 'is small molecule activator of' GOLPH3 cargo adaptor activity (IMP: Golgi PI4P depletion and PI4P-binding mutants, PMID:19837035; R90L and PIK93, PMID:42276998), PI4P located in GO:0160288 (IC)."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Built by claude4go 2026-09-23 from Rizzo et al 2021 EMBO J (PMID:33749896): GOLPH3 binds the LxxR cytosolic tails of B4GALT5, A4GALT, ST3GAL5 and ST8SIA1 and recycles them in COPI vesicles from the trans cisterna (cryo-IEM, RUSH), retaining them in the Golgi and preventing lysosomal degradation; GOLPH3 KD/OE lowers/raises LacCer, Gb3, GM3 output. Cargo adaptor MF also from Welch et al 2021 (PMID:34473204). PI4KB (1-phosphatidylinositol 4-kinase activity) directly positively regulates GOLPH3 by generating the trans-Golgi PI4P pool that recruits it (Dippold 2009 PMID:19837035; PI4KIIIbeta named as the kinase by Rizzo 2021); per project convention the kinase reaction itself (PI -> PI4P) is not described. GOLPH3->client edges are 'indirectly positively regulates' (IMP): GOLPH3 controls client localisation and level, not catalysis. Trans-cisterna location is direct (IDA) for B4GALT5 only; inferred (IC) for the three co-clients and for the lumenal location of GlcCer/LacCer/Gb3/GM3/GD3 (with Lannert 1998 PMID:9446606). Downstream Gb3->Akt/mTOR mitogenic signalling deliberately left out (mechanism unresolved)."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Curated with GO AI HUB. GOLPH3, a COPI cargo adaptor recruited by PI4P, retains the glycosphingolipid synthases B4GALT5, A4GALT, ST3GAL5 and ST8SIA1 in the trans-Golgi, controlling LacCer, Gb3, GM3 and GD3 synthesis (Rizzo 2021)."^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <https://w3id.org/biolink/vocab/in_taxon> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606> .

